SUMMARY:Applied Mathematics Seminar: Matthias Dogbatsey — A Diffuse-Inter
 face Variational Implicit Solvation Model with the Size-Modified Poisson-B
 oltzmann Equation: Formulation\, Numerical Computation\, and Stern-Layer F
 ormation
LOCATION:GP 346\, The University of Alabama\, Tuscaloosa\, Alabama
DESCRIPTION:Matthias Dogbatsey\, PhD student\, Department of Mathematics\, 
 The University of Alabama\nA Diffuse-Interface Variational Implicit Solvat
 ion Model with the Size-Modified Poisson-Boltzmann Equation: Formulation\,
  Numerical Computation\, and Stern-Layer Formation\nDiffuse-interface vari
 ational implicit solvation models (VISMs) enable efficient computation of 
 ensemble average solvation energies without costly molecular dynamics samp
 ling. However\, the underlying coupled nonlinear PDEs remain computational
 ly demanding\, and the classical Poisson–Boltzmann model neglects finite
  ion size\, predicting unphysically high concentrations near molecular sur
 faces. We present the first numerical realization of the diffuse-interface
  VISM\, developed to date only analytically\, and the first to incorporate
  steric effects via the fully nonlinear size-modified Poisson–Boltzmann 
 (SMPB) equation\, coupled to a p-Laplace equation that determines the solu
 te-solvent interface variationally rather than prescribing it. Our solver 
 combines an alternating direction implicit scheme with an inexact Newton
 –Krylov method\, stabilized by a coupling relaxation strategy. We valida
 te against manufactured solutions and biomolecular benchmarks\, and show t
 hat both steric ion effects and short-range Lennard-Jones repulsion are re
 quired for a Stern layer to emerge.\nhttps://jiazhaomath.github.io/seminar
 /2026-2027.html#2026-09-11
URL:https://jiazhaomath.github.io/seminar/2026-2027.html#2026-09-11
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
